"""Deli Counter 0.234.0: the walker's open-floor table -- each pair of rooms one floor or two (roadmap 260, from 255).

The walker, 2026-10-19: "go ahead with the 255 table, your defaults are good". Roadmap 255 left 49 open floors in 26
built specs for the walker to sort one pair at a time; they are 20 pairs of room ids, sorted here once by a table in
Deli Counter, so one row moves every building that has the pair. A wall the table builds carries a door wherever the
two rooms would otherwise lose their walkable way through, and every door opening ships to gameplay as a door socket.
Measured first: `docs/findings/open_floor_table_260/` (pairs.py; the census before and after).

What it changes (anchored; each file pinned by hash; nothing written on a miss; every file LF):
  * open_floor_rules.py (new) -- RULES, DOORWAY_POLICY, apply(): OPEN names the floor, WALL closes each uncovered
    stretch (a partition run on, its openings kept where built, or a piece of its own), slides an opening a new wall's
    end would split (L18), puts one door where the pair would lose its walkable way, never into an objective, and takes
    a pair back whole when it would leave the spec failing a lint rule it passed.
  * migrate_open_floor_rules.py (new) -- the library migration; test_open_floor_rules.py (new, 11).
  * tactical.py -- exterior_parts and exterior_sides; build_graph counts exterior walls; its docstring's return.
  * layout_lint.py -- _story_parts counts exterior walls (_exterior_sides); L26's message offers the table.
  * spec_types.py -- Room.open_to (the schema had it; the loader refused it).
  * presets.py -- make() applies the table and trims a piece the new wall runs through.
  * build_freshness.py -- open_floor_rules.py a geometry source.
  * open_floor_baseline.py -- its reason says the table sorted it.
  * walk_reach_baseline.json -- rowhouse_raid's vault, the objective, by the walker's rule.
  * test_open_floor.py, test_wall_over_void.py, test_stair_back.py -- see the CHANGELOG.
  * VERSION 0.233.0 -> 0.234.0, CHANGELOG.

AFTER APPLYING, in deli_counter/: migrate_open_floor_rules.py (23 specs), migrate_furnish_recipes.py (three move),
open_floor_baseline.py (empty), catalog.py, the suite, build.py --all (presets.py and the specs moved), check.py.

    python patches/patch_dc_open_floor_table.py --tests   # the test file only (prove it fails first)
    python patches/patch_dc_open_floor_table.py           # everything
"""
